  "whyItMatters": "Members of finite stiffness do not enforce rigid-body motion: the connected nodes can move relative to each other, so load is shared according to the flexibility of the connecting members instead of the rigid-body rule. Unlike a diaphragm, the stand-in members also couple the out-of-plane DOFs, and they have self weight and are design members like any other.",
